CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ downcast from a virtual base: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ failing downcast: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ repeated base: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ containing subobject: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [expr.dynamic.cast]/9: the run-time check applies to an operand in
a virtual base subobject (A of D : B, C with `virtual A') and to a most
derived object with several subobjects of the operand's class (two X of
M : L, R); /9.1 selects the C object derived from the subobject the
operand points to.  runtime_dynamic_cast gave up on these layouts,
leaving the nondeterministic model (bin53 rejected the program).  In a
complete object every subobject, also in a virtual base, has a fixed
offset, so each A subobject is now a case of its own, recognized by the
value its vtable pointer holds.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this
program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
